    "symptom": "the probe-estimated prior accuracy is 1.3 to 1.7 percent, far below the true prior accuracy of 9 to 11 percent, and the decision to personalise fires in 94 to 97 percent of cases",
    "cause": "PROBE was set to 20, exactly equal to K. Taking the top-K of a 20-key probe selects every probe key, so the estimate is the base rate of the pool (about 1.4 percent), not the precision@20 of the prior. With an estimate of 1.4 percent the threshold of 9.5 percent trivially fires, so the adaptive arm collapses onto the always-personalise arm.",
